---
name: wikimedia-photos-via-chrome
description: "Commons photo downloads for stops: scripts get HTTP 429, the user's Chrome works (with their OK per batch)"
metadata:
  node_type: memory
  type: feedback
  originSessionId: 9e81937d-309b-4c6b-b1d5-aba6e1a64c2b
  modified: 2026-11-19T08:56:25.007Z
---

Scripted Wikimedia image downloads (generic UA) got HTTP 429; the Commons API itself works. On 2026-11-18 the user approved fetching the stop photos through their Chrome (Claude in Chrome: navigate to the upload.wikimedia.org file, fetch → blob → `<a download>`), and they clicked Chrome's "allow multiple downloads" prompt themselves.

**Why:** spoofing a browser UA in a script was refused as unauthorized; the user's real browser at human pace is fine.
On 2026-11-19 Chrome silently blocked every download after the first in a batch; what worked was fetching all files on an upload.wikimedia.org page (API via `origin=*`), packing them into one tar in JS, and downloading that single file.

**How to apply:** still ask before each new download batch (names, source, size). Use upload.wikimedia.org paths (thumbs live under /thumb/ there too). Move the files out of ~/Downloads into the scratchpad afterwards. In Chrome, call the Commons API with fetch from a commons.wikimedia.org page (works where scripts are throttled); the extension blocks results containing URLs with query strings, so return titles/paths only.
// Open and locked differentials. Pure: no DOM, no three.js. Units: m, s, N, rad/s.

// Cornering: each driven wheel follows its own circle about the turn centre, so the outer wheel turns faster.
// radius = turn radius at the axle centre (m, + = turning left, Infinity = straight), v = axle-centre speed (m/s).
// diff = half the speed difference: the side gears' speed relative to the carrier, which the spider gears take up.
export function cornerSpeeds({ halfTrack, wheelR }, radius, v) {
  const k = Number.isFinite(radius) ? halfTrack / radius : 0;
  const left = v * (1 - k) / wheelR, right = v * (1 + k) / wheelR;
  return { left, right, carrier: (left + right) / 2, diff: (right - left) / 2 };
}

// Drive force on an axle. Open: both sides always get the same torque, so the wheel with less grip limits both.
// Locked: the axle turns as one shaft and each wheel can push up to its own grip.
// p = { torque (N·m at the axle), wheelR, normal (N per wheel), muL, muR, locked, resist (N needed to move the car) }.
export function traction({ torque, wheelR, normal, muL, muR, locked, resist = 0 }) {
  const gripL = muL * normal, gripR = muR * normal, want = torque / wheelR;
  let fL, fR, spinL, spinR;
  if (locked) {
    const grip = gripL + gripR, f = Math.min(want, grip);
    fL = grip ? f * gripL / grip : 0; fR = f - fL;
    spinL = spinR = want > grip;
  } else {
    // The wheel with less grip spins first; that caps the torque on both sides, so the other wheel never spins.
    const each = Math.min(want / 2, gripL, gripR);
    fL = fR = each;
    spinL = want / 2 > gripL && gripL <= gripR; spinR = want / 2 > gripR && gripR <= gripL;
  }
  const total = fL + fR;
  return { fL, fR, total, spinL, spinR, moves: total > resist };
}

// Four-wheel drive through three differentials: front, centre and rear, each open or locked. With traction control by the
// brakes (4ETS, brake > 0) a wheel that would spin on an open differential is braked instead, so its side of the
// differential can pass on up to `brake` more. Forces at the tyres in N, wheels ordered fl, fr, rl, rr.
// p = { force (N: the engine's drive at the wheels, all four together), normal (N per wheel), mu: [4], front, centre,
//   rear (true = locked), brake (N a wheel brake can hold back, 0 = none), resist (N needed to move the car),
//   rearOnly (front axle disengaged: part-time four-wheel drive in two-wheel mode) }.
export function traction4({ force, normal, mu, front, centre, rear, brake = 0, resist = 0, rearOnly = false }) {
  const grip = mu.map(m => m * normal);
  // One axle: input = the force put into its differential; drive = what its tyres push. Open, each side takes input/2,
  // which may be up to its grip plus what its brake can hold; locked, the sides share it in proportion to grip.
  const axle = (gL, gR, locked) => ({
    max: locked ? gL + gR : 2 * Math.min(gL, gR) + 2 * brake,
    drive: input => (locked ? Math.min(input, gL + gR) : Math.min(input / 2, gL) + Math.min(input / 2, gR)),
    locked, g: [gL, gR],
  });
  const axles = [axle(grip[0], grip[1], front), axle(grip[2], grip[3], rear)];
  let inputs;
  if (rearOnly) inputs = [0, Math.min(force, axles[1].max)];
  else if (!centre) { const i = Math.min(force / 2, axles[0].max, axles[1].max); inputs = [i, i]; }
  else {
    // Locked centre: split the input where it drives most (brakes waste whatever they hold back).
    let best = -1;
    for (let k = 0; k <= 200; k++) {
      const f = Math.min(force, axles[0].max) * k / 200, r = Math.min(force - f, axles[1].max);
      const d = axles[0].drive(f) + axles[1].drive(r);
      if (d > best + 1e-9) { best = d; inputs = [f, r]; }
    }
  }
  const drive = axles[0].drive(inputs[0]) + axles[1].drive(inputs[1]);
  const excess = force > inputs[0] + inputs[1] + 1e-6;
  // Which wheels spin: with drive left over, those of an axle that takes all it can and whose own grip (plus brake) is
  // used up. Which are braked: on an open axle, those given more than their grip.
  const spin = [], braked = [];
  axles.forEach((a, k) => a.g.forEach(g => {
    const full = inputs[k] >= a.max - 1e-6 && !(rearOnly && k === 0), side = inputs[k] / 2;
    spin.push(excess && full && (a.locked || side >= g + brake - 1e-6));
    braked.push(!a.locked && brake > 0 && side > g + 1e-6 ? Math.min(brake, side - g) : 0);
  }));
  return { drive, moves: drive > resist, spin, braked, inputs };
}
// Driven axle with an open differential: crown wheel (or belt pulley) and carrier, two spider gears on a cross pin, two
// side gears on the half-shafts. mode "corner": the outer wheel has further to go and the spider gears start to turn.
// mode "grip": one wheel on a slippery patch; open, it spins and the car stays put; locked, both wheels pull.
// Params (mm, ground at z = 0): label, mode, halfTrack, wheelR, axleX, wheel "wire" | "tyre", tyreW?, ringR,
// drive "crown" | "belt", counter? { x, z, half } (differential on a countershaft, chains to the wheels: Benz 1886),
// corner? { kmh, minRadius (m) }, grip? { torque (N·m at the axle), normal (N per wheel), muLow, muHigh, resist (N),
// surface ("ice": the slippery patch, named in the panel), locks (bool) }.
import * as THREE from "three";
import { V, mat, rod, place, tyre, wireWheel, line } from "../lib/scene/helpers.js";
import { cornerSpeeds, traction } from "../lib/model/differential.js";

const SLOW = 0.3, SIDE = 0.05, PIN = 0.045, Z_SIDE = 16, Z_SPIDER = 10;   // shown speed share; gear offsets (m); teeth

export function create(ctx, p) {
  const { stage, carRoot, t } = ctx, m = v => v / 1000;
  const SURFACE = { ice: { on: t("Left wheel, on ice"), under: t("ice under the left wheel") } };   // whole phrases: case endings differ
  const h = m(p.halfTrack), R = m(p.wheelR), ax = m(p.axleX);
  const group = new THREE.Group(); carRoot.add(group);
  const iron = mat(0x5a626b, { metalness: 0.5 }), tyreMat = mat(0x2a2d31, { roughness: 0.9 }), dark = mat(0x343b42);
  const rimMat = mat(0x5a626b, { metalness: 0.5 }), wheelMats = [tyreMat, rimMat];   // faded over the museum photo
  const sideMat = stage.tokenMat("--l1"), spiderMat = stage.tokenMat("--l2"), carrierMat = stage.tokenMat("--metal"), shaftMat = stage.tokenMat("--l4");
  const K = p.counter ? 0.22 / 0.07 : 1;   // half-shaft turns per wheel turn (chain sprockets on the countershaft)
  const cx = p.counter ? m(p.counter.x) : ax, cz = p.counter ? m(p.counter.z) : R, half = p.counter ? m(p.counter.half) : h;
  const C = V(cx, 0, cz);
  const marked = (geo, material, markSize) => {   // a part with a dark mark so its rotation is visible
    const g = new THREE.Group(); g.add(new THREE.Mesh(geo, material));
    const k = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.BoxGeometry(markSize[0], markSize[1], markSize[2]), dark); k.position.z = markSize[3] ?? 0; g.add(k); return g;
  };
  const spinner = (pos, part) => { const g = new THREE.Group(); g.position.copy(pos); g.add(part); group.add(g); return g; };

  // Wheels (axis along y) on their own spinners.
  const wheels = [1, -1].map(s => {
    const g = new THREE.Group();
    if (p.wheel === "wire") { const spokes = line(0x9aa4ad, 0.85); spokes.userData.solid = rimMat; wheelMats.push(spokes); g.add(wireWheel(tyreMat, spokes, R - 0.02, 0.02, R - 0.05, 28)); }
    else { const tw = m(p.tyreW ?? 110); g.add(tyre(tyreMat, R - tw, tw)); g.add(new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.CylinderGeometry(R - 1.8 * tw, R - 1.8 * tw, 0.14, 32), rimMat)); }
    const mk = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.BoxGeometry(0.05, 0.15, 0.45 * R), carrierMat); mk.position.z = 0.4 * R; g.add(mk);
    return spinner(V(ax, s * h, R), g);
  });

  for (const w of wheelMats) { w.transparent = true; w.userData.opacity = w.opacity; }

  // Carrier: crown wheel or belt pulley, cross pin, two spider gears. Side gears turn with their half-shafts.
  const carrier = spinner(C, new THREE.Group());
  const ringR = m(p.ringR);
  if (p.drive === "belt") carrier.add(marked(new THREE.CylinderGeometry(ringR, ringR, 0.1, 40, 1, true), new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial({ color: 0x8a6a4a, transparent: true, opacity: 0.35, side: THREE.DoubleSide, depthWrite: false }), [0.03, 0.1, 0.03, ringR]));
  else { const crown = marked(new THREE.CylinderGeometry(ringR, ringR, 0.02, 40), carrierMat, [0.03, 0.022, 0.03, ringR - 0.02]); crown.position.y = -SIDE - 0.02; carrier.add(crown); }
  carrier.add(place(rod(carrierMat, 0.008), V(0, 0, -PIN - 0.02), V(0, 0, PIN + 0.02)));
  const spiders = [1, -1].map(s => {
    const holder = new THREE.Group(); holder.position.z = s * PIN; carrier.add(holder);
    const gear = marked(new THREE.CylinderGeometry(0.018, 0.03, 0.025, 20), spiderMat, [0.012, 0.03, 0.012, 0]);
    gear.children[1].position.set(0.022, 0, 0);
    gear.rotation.x = s > 0 ? -Math.PI / 2 : Math.PI / 2; holder.add(gear); return holder;
  });
  const sides = [1, -1].map(s => {
    const gear = marked(new THREE.CylinderGeometry(s > 0 ? 0.042 : 0.028, s > 0 ? 0.028 : 0.042, 0.03, 24), sideMat, [0.012, 0.032, 0.012, 0.03]);
    return spinner(V(cx, s * SIDE, cz), gear);
  });

  // Half-shafts; with a countershaft, sprockets and a chain to each wheel.
  const chainLinks = [];
  for (const s of [1, -1]) {
    group.add(place(rod(shaftMat, 0.014), V(cx, s * SIDE, cz), V(cx, s * half, cz)));
    if (!p.counter) continue;
    const yw = s * (h - 0.09), r1 = 0.07, r2 = 0.22;
    chainLinks.push(spinner(V(cx, s * half, cz), marked(new THREE.CylinderGeometry(r1, r1, 0.02, 24), iron, [0.02, 0.022, 0.02, r1 - 0.01])));
    chainLinks.push(spinner(V(ax, yw, R), marked(new THREE.CylinderGeometry(r2, r2, 0.02, 40), iron, [0.03, 0.022, 0.03, r2 - 0.02])));
    for (const t of [1, -1]) group.add(place(rod(dark, 0.006), V(cx, s * half, cz + t * r1), V(ax, yw, R + t * r2)));
  }
  const housing = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.SphereGeometry(0.11, 24, 16), new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial({ color: 0x8fa3b3, transparent: true, opacity: 0.12, depthWrite: false }));
  housing.position.copy(C); if (p.drive !== "belt") group.add(housing);

  // Ground: wheel paths in a corner, slippery patch for the grip demo.
  const pathOf = token => { const l = new THREE.Line(new THREE.BufferGeometry().setFromPoints(Array.from({ length: 41 }, () => V(0, 0, 0))), new THREE.LineBasicMaterial()); stage.bind(l.material.color, token); l.frustumCulled = false; group.add(l); return l; };
  const paths = p.mode === "corner" ? [pathOf("--l1"), pathOf("--l2")] : [];
  const patch = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.PlaneGeometry(1.2, 0.6), new THREE.MeshBasicMaterial({ transparent: true, opacity: 0.55, depthWrite: false }));
  stage.bind(patch.material.color, "--l4"); patch.position.set(ax, h, 0.004); patch.visible = p.mode === "grip"; group.add(patch);

  // ---------- state + panel ----------
  const D = 180 / Math.PI;
  let auto = !ctx.reducedMotion, clock = 0, curve = 0.6, locked = false, angL = 0, angR = 0, angC = 0;   // half-shaft and carrier angles
  const ui = p.mode === "corner" ? ctx.panel([{ label: p.label, items: [
    { slider: { id: "curve", label: t("Steering: right ← straight → left"), min: -1, max: 1, step: 0.05, value: curve, onInput: v => { auto = false; ui.toggle("auto").set(false); curve = v; } } },
    { readouts: [{ id: "radius", label: t("Turn radius"), unit: t("m, axle centre") }, { id: "left", label: t("Left wheel"), unit: t("rpm") }, { id: "right", label: t("Right wheel"), unit: t("rpm") },
      { id: "spider", label: t("Spider gears"), unit: t("rpm in the carrier") }, { id: "extra", label: t("Outer wheel goes"), unit: t("% further") }] },
    { buttons: [{ id: "auto", toggle: [t("Auto demo on"), t("Auto demo off")], pressed: auto, onClick: v => (auto = v) }] },
    { key: [["--l1", t("left wheel path")], ["--l2", t("right wheel path")]] },
  ] }, { label: t("Parts"), items: [{ legend: [["--l1", t("Side gears (one per half-shaft)")], ["--l2", t("Spider gears")], ["--metal", p.drive === "belt" ? t("Carrier inside the belt pulley") : t("Carrier and crown wheel")], ["--l4", t("Half-shafts")]] }] }])
    : ctx.panel([{ label: p.label, badge: { id: "moves", text: "" }, items: [
      { buttons: [{ id: "open", label: t("Open differential"), pressed: true, onClick: () => setLock(false) },
        ...(p.grip.locks ? [{ id: "lock", label: t("Differential lock"), pressed: false, onClick: () => setLock(true) }] : [])] },
      { readouts: [{ id: "fL", label: SURFACE[p.grip.surface].on, unit: t("N of push") }, { id: "fR", label: t("Right wheel, dry"), unit: t("N of push") },
        { id: "total", label: t("Total drive"), unit: t("N, needs {0} to move", p.grip.resist) }, { id: "spin", label: t("Left wheel"), unit: t("rpm") }] },
      { buttons: [{ id: "auto", toggle: [t("Auto demo on"), t("Auto demo off")], pressed: auto, onClick: v => (auto = v) }] },
      { key: [["--l4", SURFACE[p.grip.surface].under]] },
    ] }, { label: t("Parts"), items: [{ legend: [["--l1", t("Side gears (one per half-shaft)")], ["--l2", t("Spider gears")], ["--metal", t("Carrier and crown wheel")], ["--l4", t("Half-shafts")]] }] }]);
  function setLock(v) { locked = v; ui.toggle("open").set(!v); if (p.grip.locks) ui.toggle("lock").set(v); }

  const rpm = w => (w * 60 / (2 * Math.PI)).toFixed(0);
  function corner(dt) {
    if (auto) { clock += dt; curve = Math.sin(0.35 * clock); ui.slider("curve").set(curve.toFixed(2)); }
    const radius = Math.abs(curve) < 0.02 ? Infinity : p.corner.minRadius / curve, v = p.corner.kmh / 3.6;
    const s = cornerSpeeds({ halfTrack: h, wheelR: R }, radius, v);
    angL += s.left * K * SLOW * dt; angR += s.right * K * SLOW * dt; angC += s.carrier * K * SLOW * dt;
    const straight = !Number.isFinite(radius);
    [h, -h].forEach((y, i) => {   // each wheel's path, 4 m ahead
      const pos = paths[i].geometry.attributes.position;
      for (let k = 0; k <= 40; k++) {
        const d = k / 40 * 4;
        if (straight) pos.setXYZ(k, ax + d, y, 0.01);
        else { const rr = radius - y, a = d / Math.abs(rr); pos.setXYZ(k, ax + rr * Math.sin(a) * Math.sign(rr), radius - rr * Math.cos(a), 0.01); }
      }
      pos.needsUpdate = true;
    });
    ui.set("radius", straight ? t("straight") : Math.abs(radius).toFixed(1));
    ui.set("left", rpm(s.left)); ui.set("right", rpm(s.right));
    ui.set("spider", rpm(Math.abs(s.diff) * Z_SIDE / Z_SPIDER));
    ui.set("extra", straight ? "0" : ((Math.max(s.left, s.right) / Math.min(s.left, s.right) - 1) * 100).toFixed(0));
  }
  function grip(dt) {
    if (auto) { clock += dt; const lk = p.grip.locks && Math.floor(clock / 5) % 2 === 1; if (lk !== locked) setLock(lk); }
    const g = p.grip, r = traction({ torque: g.torque, wheelR: R, normal: g.normal, muL: g.muLow, muR: g.muHigh, locked, resist: g.resist });
    const wC = 1.2 / R;   // carrier speed from the engine: walking pace, as on a slippery start
    // Open with the left wheel slipping: the right wheel stands and the left one turns twice as fast as the carrier.
    const [wL, wR] = locked ? [wC, wC] : r.spinL ? [2 * wC, 0] : r.moves ? [wC, wC] : [0, 0];
    angL += wL * K * SLOW * dt; angR += wR * K * SLOW * dt; angC += (wL + wR) / 2 * K * SLOW * dt;
    ui.set("fL", r.fL.toFixed(0)); ui.set("fR", r.fR.toFixed(0)); ui.set("total", r.total.toFixed(0)); ui.set("spin", rpm(wL));
    ui.badge("moves").set(r.moves ? t("Car moves off") : t("Stuck: left wheel spins"), r.moves);
  }

  return {
    layout({ active, onPhoto }) {
      group.visible = active;
      for (const w of wheelMats) w.opacity = onPhoto ? 0.12 : w.userData.opacity;   // the real wheels show through
    },
    update(dt) {
      (p.mode === "corner" ? corner : grip)(dt);
      wheels[0].rotation.y = angL / K; wheels[1].rotation.y = angR / K;
      sides[0].rotation.y = angL; sides[1].rotation.y = angR;
      carrier.rotation.y = angC;
      const rel = (angL - angC) * Z_SIDE / Z_SPIDER;
      spiders[0].rotation.z = rel; spiders[1].rotation.z = -rel;
      chainLinks.forEach((c, i) => (c.rotation.y = (i < 2 ? angL : angR) / (i % 2 ? K : 1)));   // [left small, left big, right small, right big]
    },
  };
}
// Benz Patent-Motorwagen, 1886. Frame: mm, x forward, y left, z up; origin = rear axle centre on the ground.
// Wheel sizes, track, engine and countershaft positions, conrod and flywheel size are illustrative.
export default {
  slug: "patent-motorwagen",
  title: "The first car's engine and differential",
  name: "Benz Patent-Motorwagen",
  year: 1886,
  summary: "Karl Benz's three-wheeler: one cylinder lying flat, a horizontal flywheel, and a differential so the rear wheels can turn at different speeds.",
  eyebrow: "Benz Patent-Motorwagen, 1886",
  lede: "The car Karl Benz patented in January 1886. Watch its single cylinder lying flat at the back, then the differential on the countershaft letting the outer rear wheel run faster in a bend.",
  frame: { origin: "rear", wheelbase: 1450, wheelR: 560 },
  orbit: { min: 0.6, max: 12 },
  sun: [2, -3, 6],
  body: {
    ghost: [
      { pts: [[-100, 900], [650, 900], [650, 1130], [30, 1180], [30, 1360], [-60, 1360], [-100, 1130]], y: [-450, 450] },     // seat and box below
      { pts: [[650, 700], [1100, 700], [1100, 760], [650, 760]], y: [-300, 300] },                                           // footboard
      { torus: { R: 545, r: 15, pos: [0, 600, 560], rot: [90, 0, 0] }, mirror: true },                                        // rear wheels
      { pts: [[-600, 640], [1500, 640], [1500, 680], [-600, 680]], y: [470, 510], mirror: true },                                       // frame tubes
      { torus: { R: 360, r: 16, pos: [1450, 0, 375], rot: [90, 0, 0] } },                                                                // front wheel
      { cyl: { r: [14, 14], h: 580, axis: "z", pos: [950, 0, 1000] } },                                                                // steering column
    ],
  },
  photo: {
    src: "photo.jpg", w: 1200, h: 803,
    alt: "Green-wheeled 1886 Benz Patent-Motorwagen on display in the Mercedes-Benz Museum, seen from the rear left",
    cam: { c: [-2030.4, 5338.1, 2032.2], yaw: -1.1709, pitch: -0.2016, roll: -0.0083, f: 2078.7 }, // tools/photo-fits/patent-motorwagen.json
    credit: { author: "Valder137", license: "CC BY 2.0", url: "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:REDACTED(14797106387).jpg" },
  },
  components: [
    {
      id: "engine", label: "Engine", subsystem: "inline-engine",
      view: { pos: [1.1, -1.5, 1.4], target: [-0.15, 0, 0.55] },
      ghost: { fill: 0.03, edge: 0.3 },
      params: {
        label: "Single cylinder, lying flat",
        order: [1], bore: 90, stroke: 150, rod: 300,         // rod illustrative
        xs: [-280], crankZ: 700, lean: 0,                 // placed from the photo
        rot: [180, 90, 0],                                  // cylinder pointing forward, crank vertical, flywheel underneath
        flywheelR: 340,                                     // illustrative, scaled from the photo
        valvetrain: "none", ignition: "spark", fuel: "carb", crankcase: "open",
        speed: { min: 5, max: 60, value: 20 }, realRpm: 400,
      },
      talk: [
        "One cylinder of 954 cm³ (90 × 150 mm) lies flat at the back and gives 0.75 hp at about 400 rpm.",
        "The big flywheel lies flat as well. Benz did that so its gyroscopic effect would not fight the steering in tight bends.",
        "Benz used electric ignition with a coil and a spark plug instead of Daimler's hot tube.",
        "The model shows only the piston, crank and flywheel. The real engine also has valve gear, not drawn here: Mercedes-Benz describes an intake slide and a controlled exhaust valve.",
        "The whole transmission is a belt to a countershaft: one speed and no reverse. Pushing the belt onto a loose pulley next to the drive pulley is the clutch.",
      ],
    },
    {
      id: "diff", label: "Differential", subsystem: "differential",
      view: { pos: [1.9, -2.0, 2.3], target: [0.15, 0, 0.45] },
      ghost: { fill: 0.03, edge: 0.3 },
      params: {
        label: "Differential on the countershaft", mode: "corner",
        halfTrack: 600, wheelR: 560, axleX: 0, wheel: "wire",            // illustrative
        ringR: 110, drive: "belt", counter: { x: 450, z: 450, half: 470 }, // illustrative
        corner: { kmh: 12, minRadius: 3 },
      },
      talk: [
        "In a bend the outer rear wheel has further to go than the inner one. On one solid shaft one of them would have to skid.",
        "Benz built a differential into the countershaft. The belt turns its housing, and small bevel gears inside let the two output shafts run at different speeds.",
        "From each end of the countershaft a chain runs to a rear wheel, as on a bicycle.",
        "Move the steering slider. Straight ahead the small spider gears ride round with the housing without turning; in a bend they start to spin.",
      ],
    },
  ],
  note: "Patent DRP 37435 of 29 January 1886 is often called the birth certificate of the car. Some sources give 91.4 × 150 mm (984 cm³) for the engine.",
  unverified: ["Wheel sizes, track and wheelbase", "Conrod length, flywheel size, engine and countershaft positions", "Sprocket sizes and the 12 km/h cornering speed", "Ghost-body outline (traced from the photo)"],
  sources: [
    { label: "Mercedes-Benz: Benz Patent Motor Car", url: "https://mercedes-benz.com/en/innovation/milestones/benz-patent-motor-car" },
    { label: "Wikipedia: Benz Patent-Motorwagen", url: "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Benz_Patent-Motorwagen" },
    { label: "Wheelsjoint: Benz Patent Motor Car number 1", url: "https://www.wheelsjoint.com/benz-patent-motor-car-number-1-worlds-first-automobile-with-a-combustion-engine/" },
  ],
